{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01491",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.92,
      "end_seconds": 7.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.99,
      "text": "Hello doctor, sorry, I took a wrong turn on the way here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.99,
      "end_seconds": 12.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.89,
      "end_seconds": 22.91,
      "duration_seconds": 9.02,
      "text": "Yeah, it's a painful rash on one side of my chest. I don't know what's causing it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.93,
      "end_seconds": 28.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Alright, how long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.75,
      "end_seconds": 44.79,
      "duration_seconds": 14.04,
      "text": "Erm, it's been like this since yesterday. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.4,
      "end_seconds": 52.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Does anything set it off?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.41,
      "end_seconds": 58.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Touch and clothes rubbing definitely sets it off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.04,
      "end_seconds": 62.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "How much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.16,
      "end_seconds": 69.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "It's mild, honestly. I've also been feeling feverish, for about four days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.67,
      "end_seconds": 74.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "How strong would you say it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.68,
      "end_seconds": 83.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Mostly moderate. And small blisters in a band, too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.97,
      "end_seconds": 89.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "Can I check a few measurements before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.74,
      "end_seconds": 99.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.76,
      "end_seconds": 127.59,
      "duration_seconds": 7.83,
      "text": "Okay: temperature 38.0, blood pressure 106 over 78. And heart rate 102, saturation 95 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.29,
      "end_seconds": 130.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.43,
      "end_seconds": 139.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "They help me see the whole picture, more shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.12,
      "end_seconds": 144.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.17,
      "end_seconds": 155.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Yeah, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.58,
      "end_seconds": 159.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.05,
      "end_seconds": 179.76,
      "duration_seconds": 10.71,
      "text": "There are clustered blisters on a red base in a band across the right side of the chest, not crossing the midline."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.72,
      "end_seconds": 191.9,
      "duration_seconds": 8.18,
      "text": "Alright, you can relax now. Let me check a few things. Any confusion, vision changes or rash near the eye?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.31,
      "end_seconds": 197.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "No, um, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.65,
      "end_seconds": 199.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "How about contact with chickenpox?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.45,
      "end_seconds": 205.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any contact with chickenpox."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.25,
      "end_seconds": 208.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Ah. Is your digestion otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.62,
      "end_seconds": 212.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "No, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.34,
      "end_seconds": 228.64,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.52,
      "end_seconds": 233.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "No, nothing as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.29,
      "end_seconds": 237.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Any past operations I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.18,
      "end_seconds": 242.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "Just a meniscus repair on my knee, four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.64,
      "end_seconds": 248.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.86,
      "end_seconds": 264.83,
      "duration_seconds": 9.97,
      "text": "Uh, I've had high blood pressure for two years now. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.81,
      "end_seconds": 269.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.85,
      "end_seconds": 282.62,
      "duration_seconds": 11.77,
      "text": "I work in accounts at a hospital. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.65,
      "end_seconds": 292.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.66,
      "end_seconds": 298.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "It's lisinopril, 10 milligrams, once a day for my pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.29,
      "end_seconds": 316.62,
      "duration_seconds": 13.33,
      "text": "So, to recap quickly. You've had a painful rash on one side of your chest, since yesterday, mild, and no rash near the eye or vision changes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 317.15,
      "end_seconds": 317.85,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Correct."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.45,
      "end_seconds": 353.62,
      "duration_seconds": 31.17,
      "text": "Let's get a swab from a blister, for vesicular rash. I'd like you to take aciclovir, 800 milligrams, five times a day, for seven days. It's for shingles. Keep the rash clean and dry and avoid contact with pregnant women or newborns until the blisters crust over. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.05,
      "end_seconds": 361.08,
      "duration_seconds": 7.03,
      "text": "Ah. Let me check I've been clear. What will you do once you get home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 364.2,
      "end_seconds": 372.68,
      "duration_seconds": 8.48,
      "text": "So, you know, I take the aciclovir, 800 milligrams, five times a day. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 374.38,
      "end_seconds": 378.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 379.53,
      "end_seconds": 382.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}